{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5JsygLmrz3gUTemLdx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug in `django/forms/widgets.py`. The form from the issue now produces `['text-editor.js', 'text-editor-extras.js', 'color-picker.js']` with no warning; I ran it with warnings set to raise errors.\n\n**15 existing tests now fail** across `forms_tests`, `admin_inlines` and `admin_widgets`. I believe these match how Django updated the same tests when it fixed this issue upstream, but that is from memory and I couldn't check it here. I didn't edit any test files, as the rules require. The failures are expected:\n- **Ordering:** when lists share nothing, items are now interleaved. `merge([1, 2], [3, 4])` gives `[1, 3, 2, 4]` instead of `[1, 2, 3, 4]`. The admin inline test also gets a different but valid file order.\n- **Warning text:** the conflict warning now lists all the input lists, e.g. `... opposite order: [1, 2], [2, 1]`, instead of naming one pair. The old pair was often the wrong one, as the issue points out.\n- **List vs tuple:** the autocomplete widget tests compare `_js` against a tuple, and `_js` now always returns a list.\n\n**Cause:** media lists were merged two at a time. Merging `ColorPicker` and `SimpleTextWidget` first produced `['color-picker.js', 'text-editor.js']`. That falsely required `color-picker.js` to come before `text-editor.js`, which then clashed with `FancyTextWidget`'s own order.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`merge()`** now takes all the lists at once. It records only the real \"A comes before B\" pairs from each list and orders the files to satisfy all of them, using Django's existing `stable_topological_sort`. It warns only when the pairs truly contradict each other, and then falls back to the order in which files first appear.\n- **`_js` / `_css`** pass all collected lists to that single merge. For CSS this happens once per media type.\n- **`__add__`** no longer adds empty lists or lists it already has, so the same widget's media isn't counted twice."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":29506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":341},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f17d721b-b7d5-488d-a9cb-81b71988662b","uuid":"490bd5fa-6ea1-4377-a301-1679f089346d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:31:39.736Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5JsqkAquWtKzRu2e9n"}
